  "query_preview": "../Tuesday to Saturday/ A weakening low that is \nanchored in the gulf Tuesday dissipating as it drifts north and\nmelts into the central gulf coast by Wednesday morning. Another\nlow moving NE out of the Pacific looks to move over the Haida \nGwaii or BC coast region Thursday rain may cover the southern \npanhandle, but another feature will drop into the northern gulf \nand will track east over the northern panhandle into Friday. \n\nThere does look to be a stronger low moving into the western gulf\nwith associated frontal band arcing to the central gulf by\nSaturday with 20 to 30 kt approaching the gulf coastal zones\nSaturday to Saturday night.  \n\nOverall the end of the weeks forecast will stay on the wet side\nwith fairly continuous rain, with better amounts associated to \nthe frontal bands and lows.",
